    "body": "## Description\n\n`VLLMBridgeBackend.build_generation_request` (v2 inference service) builds its vLLM payload without `gconfig.frequency_penalty` and `gconfig.stop`. The sibling `SGLangBridgeBackend` and the v1 `VLLMBackend` both forward them (the v1 backend was fixed for the same omission in #1429), and vLLM's `/v1/completions` and `/v1/chat/completions` endpoints accept both fields. So with the v2 inference service on vLLM, a configured repetition penalty and stop strings are silently ignored, and the same config samples differently depending on the backend.\n\nThis adds `frequency_penalty` to the payload, and `stop` when it is set, matching the v1 vLLM backend.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nNone found (searched open and closed issues and PRs).\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix\n- [ ] ✨ New feature\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [ ] ✅ Test coverage improvement\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/areal-project/community/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`). I ran `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` on the changed files only.\n- [x] Relevant tests pass; new tests added for new functionality\n- [ ] Documentation updated (if applicable; built with `./docs/build_all.sh`)\n- [x] Branch is up to date with `main`\n- [ ] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command\n- [ ] This PR was created by a coding agent via `/create-pr`\n- [ ] This PR is a breaking change\n\n**Breaking Change Details (if applicable):**\n\nN/A\n\n## Additional Context\n\nThe new test `test_vllm_build_generation_request_forwards_frequency_penalty_and_stop` in `tests/v2/inference_service/test_inf_bridge.py` fails on `main` with `KeyError: 'frequency_penalty'` and passes with the fix. `tests/v2/inference_service/test_inf_bridge.py` and `tests/test_vllm_generation_request.py` pass (32 tests, CPU only).\n\nAI use: I used an AI coding assistant (Claude Code) while writing the fix and tests; I reviewed the changes and ran the checks listed above.\n",
